      "content": "Yes, we can. Think of the distance formula as a shortcut across a rectangular field. If you walk 5 blocks east and 3 blocks north, the straight-line distance is the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle.\n\nThe distance formula is: $d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$.\n\nUsing your coordinates $P(1; 0)$ and $Q(6; 3)$, what do you get when you subtract the x-values and the y-values?"
