      "content": "The midpoint formula is used to find the coordinates of the point exactly in the middle of a line, not the length of the line itself. To find the length (distance) between two points $(x_1; y_1)$ and $(x_2; y_2)$, we use the distance formula: \n$$d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$$\n\nUsing this formula, what is the length of $PQ$?"
